%% alt: Sequence diagram of load_listings. The caller asks load_listings for a file. The function reads every column as text with pandas, calls coerce for each column to get typed values and the cells that failed to parse, calls validate with the schema, and returns the typed DataFrame together with a report. The caller then decides: on STOP it raises an error that carries the report; otherwise it goes on with the analysis.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant U as Caller
  participant L as load_listings
  participant P as pandas
  participant C as coerce
  participant V as validate
  U->>+L: load_listings(path)
  L->>P: read_csv(dtype=str)
  P-->>L: every cell as text
  loop each column
    L->>C: coerce(text, rule)
    C-->>L: typed column, failed cells
  end
  L->>V: validate(df, schema)
  V-->>L: list of problems
  L-->>-U: df, report
  alt decide(problems) is STOP
    Note over U: raise an error<br/>that carries the report
  else GO or GO WITH CARE
    Note over U: continue with the analysis
  end
